Expose the Talker's context, so the cost of speech can be split.

The omni lane measured about 3x slower than real time on a desktop, and the one
lever on that which does not need a different model is dit_steps -- MNN runs
`steps - 1` DiT forwards per 1.2 s chunk, and the shipped config says 5. Whether
turning it is worth anything depends on how much of the 3x is the diffusion
sampler, and nothing reachable from outside MNN said.

The reason is that the Talker is a separate Llm with a separate LlmContext. The
counters on the engine's own context -- prefill_us, decode_us, audio_us -- cover
the thinker alone; the Talker's carries its prefill, its autoregressive decode,
and token2wav (the DiT sampler plus BigVGAN) in audio_us. A host can therefore
time the whole exchange and cannot say which part of it to attack.

MNN already computes exactly this split under DUMP_TALKER_PERFORMANCE, which
prints it to stdout of a debug build. This adds one virtual so the same numbers
reach a host: getTalkerContext(), NULL on an engine without a Talker.

Note that generate_init() resets prefill_us, decode_us and sample_us but NOT
audio_us, so a caller wanting per-exchange token2wav time has to snapshot it
before generation and subtract.

diff --git a/transformers/llm/engine/include/llm/llm.hpp b/transformers/llm/engine/include/llm/llm.hpp
index ead27da..720495e 100644
--- a/transformers/llm/engine/include/llm/llm.hpp
+++ b/transformers/llm/engine/include/llm/llm.hpp
@@ -215,6 +215,20 @@ public:
     const LlmContext* getContext() const {
         return mContext.get();
     }
+    // The Talker's context, for an engine that owns one. NULL otherwise.
+    //
+    // The Talker is a separate Llm with a separate LlmContext, so none of its
+    // work appears in the counters above: this engine's context reports the
+    // thinker alone. The Talker's carries the three numbers that say where the
+    // cost of speech went -- prefill_us, decode_us for its autoregressive half,
+    // and audio_us for token2wav, which is the DiT sampler plus the vocoder.
+    //
+    // That split is what decides whether dit_steps is worth turning, and
+    // DUMP_TALKER_PERFORMANCE already prints it; this exposes the same numbers
+    // to a host rather than to stdout of a debug build.
+    virtual const LlmContext* getTalkerContext() const {
+        return nullptr;
+    }
     const std::shared_ptr<Express::Executor>& getExecutor() const {
         return mExecutor;
     }
